    Examples::

        >>> a = tensorplay.randn(4)
        >>> a
        tensor([ 0.0202,  1.0985,  1.3506, -0.6056])
        >>> tensorplay.add(a, 20)
        tensor([ 20.0202,  21.0985,  21.3506,  19.3944])

        >>> b = tensorplay.randn(4)
        >>> b
        tensor([-0.9732, -0.3497,  0.6245,  0.4022])
        >>> c = tensorplay.randn(4, 1)
